The chart is published to OCI as <registry>/k0sproject/k0smotron-chart, and
`helm push` derives that repository name from Chart.yaml's `name`. The scaffolded
"chart.name" helper feeds .Chart.Name into app.kubernetes.io/name (and into the
manager Deployment's immutable selector), so without this patch every object
would be labelled "k0smotron-chart".

The edit drops the .Chart.Name branch so the helper resolves to .Values.nameOverride
or the constant "k0smotron", decoupling the published artifact name from the
in-cluster labels.

Like manager.patch, `make helm-chart` deletes the file first so the plugin writes
a pristine copy, then applies this on top. If a kubebuilder bump changes the
scaffold, `git apply` fails loudly; refresh by editing the generated file and
re-diffing it against a pristine scaffold.

diff --git a/dist/chart/templates/_helpers.tpl b/dist/chart/templates/_helpers.tpl
index b0d9081..c1ed9be 100644
--- a/dist/chart/templates/_helpers.tpl
+++ b/dist/chart/templates/_helpers.tpl
@@ -1,14 +1,8 @@
 {{- define "chart.name" -}}
-{{- if .Chart }}
-  {{- if .Chart.Name }}
-    {{- .Chart.Name | trunc 63 | trimSuffix "-" }}
-  {{- else if .Values.nameOverride }}
-    {{ .Values.nameOverride | trunc 63 | trimSuffix "-" }}
-  {{- else }}
-    k0smotron
-  {{- end }}
+{{- if .Values.nameOverride }}
+  {{- .Values.nameOverride | trunc 63 | trimSuffix "-" }}
 {{- else }}
-  k0smotron
+  {{- "k0smotron" }}
 {{- end }}
 {{- end }}
 
